WEBVTT

00:02.900 --> 00:04.740
A long, long time ago.

00:04.960 --> 00:07.640
A story from about a hundred years ago.

00:08.530 --> 00:13.280
Nadja, guided by
destiny, arrived in France.

00:17.480 --> 00:18.780
- NAAJA
- Nadja,

00:18.900 --> 00:20.170
With your eyes

00:20.171 --> 00:21.439
Kimi no hitomi ni wa

00:21.440 --> 00:22.650
- Nadja,
- NAAJA

00:22.690 --> 00:23.820
What do you see?

00:23.821 --> 00:24.950
Nani ga mieru

00:24.980 --> 00:26.425
Haruka tooku hikaru

00:26.426 --> 00:27.870
Shining in the far distance,

00:27.880 --> 00:29.070
The door to the future,

00:29.071 --> 00:30.260
Mirai no tobira

00:31.140 --> 00:32.880
That's what I'm searching for

00:32.881 --> 00:34.619
Sagashite iru

00:34.620 --> 00:38.230
Tomorrow's Nadja

00:42.540 --> 00:44.300
If everyone could meet with a smile

00:44.301 --> 00:46.060
Minna egao de aetara

00:46.140 --> 00:49.390
- I'm sure there would be no more fighting
- Arasoi mo kitto nakunaru

00:49.420 --> 00:51.025
It could be so much more fun

00:51.026 --> 00:52.630
Konna ni mo tanoshi kunaru

00:52.690 --> 00:54.400
The world is wide, but it's still one

00:54.401 --> 00:56.110
Sekai wa hiroi kedo hitotsu ne

00:56.470 --> 00:58.120
I can't see the end of the journey

00:58.121 --> 00:59.770
Tabi no owari wa mienai

00:59.890 --> 01:03.220
- God is the only one who could
possibly know - Kamisama ga tabun shitteru

01:03.410 --> 01:07.000
- To the people who, someday, I will meet
again - Itsukamata deaeru hito tachi ni

01:07.040 --> 01:08.100
I will go waving

01:08.101 --> 01:09.160
Te wo furinagara

01:09.240 --> 01:12.570
Sometimes, there are days I feel blue,

01:12.571 --> 01:15.900
Toki ni wa BURUU ni naru hi mo aru kedo

01:15.970 --> 01:17.325
But I won't look back

01:17.326 --> 01:18.680
Ushiro mukanai

01:19.010 --> 01:21.490
Until the day my dream comes true

01:21.491 --> 01:23.970
Yume ga kanau hi made

01:24.260 --> 01:25.970
Nadja, Your smile

01:25.971 --> 01:27.680
NAAJA kimi no hohoemi wa

01:27.740 --> 01:29.410
Nadja, gives me courage

01:29.411 --> 01:31.080
NAAJA yuuki ni naru

01:31.150 --> 01:32.610
Under the blue sky,

01:32.611 --> 01:34.070
Aoi sora no shita de

01:34.170 --> 01:35.585
I will find the place

01:35.586 --> 01:37.000
Ashita no yukue

01:37.330 --> 01:39.285
where my future lies

01:39.286 --> 01:41.240
Mitsukeru kara

01:48.240 --> 01:51.640
Thank you, thank you, thank you very much!

01:51.730 --> 01:55.059
People of Australia!

01:55.060 --> 01:56.060
Thank you very much!

01:56.061 --> 01:57.719
Tak, tak, thank you very much!

01:57.720 --> 01:58.720
Thank you very much!!

01:59.010 --> 02:01.539
People of Denmark!

02:01.540 --> 02:04.750
Now, our people will go
around amongst you.

02:04.751 --> 02:09.400
Dankeschön, dankeschön, thank
you very much! People of Austria

02:04.820 --> 02:07.320
We thank you for your donations.

02:08.460 --> 02:09.840
Thank you very much!

02:09.841 --> 02:16.480
Dank u wel, dank u wel, thank
you very much! People of Holland!

02:10.180 --> 02:11.420
You are welcome.

02:13.250 --> 02:14.370
Thank you!

02:15.260 --> 02:16.550
Thank you very much!

02:16.551 --> 02:20.020
Lala-lalala, lala-lalala,
lala, let's dance!

02:16.880 --> 02:18.140
Please visit us again.

02:18.160 --> 02:19.200
Nadja!

02:20.070 --> 02:23.640
Lala-lalala, lala-lalala, lala, let's sing!

02:20.160 --> 02:21.910
Herbie! TJ!

02:23.530 --> 02:25.280
That sure was a pretty dance.

02:25.281 --> 02:27.140
Girls and boys. Señorita, Señor.

02:27.200 --> 02:30.639
Some day, some day, we will meet again!

02:30.640 --> 02:31.640
Thank you!

02:37.370 --> 02:38.750
What is it? What is it, Granny?

02:38.920 --> 02:41.420
This is our largest earnings
since coming to Paris!

02:41.480 --> 02:42.480
Really?!

02:42.610 --> 02:43.940
That's great isn't it?

02:44.060 --> 02:46.440
A huge crowd did come to see
us today, don't you think?

02:46.890 --> 02:48.600
Well lately we've been doing great...

02:48.760 --> 02:50.260
How about we take a day off tomorrow?

02:50.670 --> 02:51.840
Really?!

02:52.610 --> 02:57.000
Bravo! All right! All right!

03:03.860 --> 03:08.660
The Music Box with Memories of Two

03:08.960 --> 03:10.720
Cheers!!

03:13.450 --> 03:15.320
Eh? The flea market?

03:15.840 --> 03:18.550
Tomorrow, TJ and I have
the day off too, so...

03:21.800 --> 03:23.510
I wondered why not go together?

03:23.560 --> 03:28.060
Used clothes, used clocks, even used
gramophones, there are some real bargains.

03:28.290 --> 03:29.340
Let's go together!

03:29.650 --> 03:31.400
Clocks and gramophones?

03:31.440 --> 03:32.840
Sounds fun!

03:33.300 --> 03:34.760
Sure, I'll go!

03:34.930 --> 03:36.240
You're going too right, Rita?

03:37.310 --> 03:38.810
Hello?

03:39.260 --> 03:41.350
I didn't invite you.

03:41.370 --> 03:44.170
I don't want to go with you either!

03:44.520 --> 03:47.070
But, seeing as Herbie kindly
invited me, I'll go.

03:47.430 --> 03:48.560
What?!

03:48.690 --> 03:49.690
Want to fight?!

03:50.360 --> 03:51.950
STOP~!

03:52.670 --> 03:54.460
If you're going to fight, I won't go!

03:54.610 --> 03:55.610
Right, Rita?

03:56.660 --> 03:59.700
Come on now! We were just
kidding around! Right, TJ?

03:59.930 --> 04:03.390
Yeah! It may not look it,
but we're best buddies!

04:05.400 --> 04:06.740
You bet!

04:20.150 --> 04:24.780
In the building we just passed, lays
the body of the famous Napoleon.

04:25.030 --> 04:28.370
The guy who said, "The word impossible
is not in my dictionary"...

04:28.410 --> 04:29.660
France's hero, right?

04:29.750 --> 04:32.790
You sure do know your stuff
for someone who's Japanese.

04:32.810 --> 04:33.580
Yeah well...

04:33.610 --> 04:35.560
Oh, Kennosuke...

04:35.920 --> 04:38.840
Master told you about that
when we came to Paris.

04:39.360 --> 04:40.450
Nadja...

04:40.560 --> 04:42.720
I knew it had to be something like that!

04:43.690 --> 04:45.260
You're laughing too much.

04:45.580 --> 04:47.120
Hey, what do you think you're doing?!

04:48.760 --> 04:50.560
If you're going to
quarrel, we're going home.

04:52.100 --> 04:53.600
It's a joke, a joke!

04:53.650 --> 04:55.900
Yeah, yeah. We're best buddies, aren't we!

04:56.280 --> 04:57.280
Right?!

05:14.530 --> 05:17.820
When you talk about Parisian flea markets,
the Clignancourt is the most famous.

05:18.170 --> 05:20.760
But, I like Vanves over here better.

05:23.900 --> 05:25.150
It's so pretty, isn't it!

05:28.350 --> 05:29.020
Huh?

05:29.250 --> 05:30.250
What's the matter?

05:30.520 --> 05:32.150
Isn't that the Master?

05:33.080 --> 05:34.130
It looks like him...

05:45.220 --> 05:48.060
Is this a real treasure map?

05:48.410 --> 05:50.290
If you're doubtful, I won't sell it to you.

05:50.400 --> 05:52.480
W-W-W-Wait a second!

05:56.110 --> 05:57.860
Master! What are you buying?

05:58.260 --> 05:59.550
N-N-Nadja!

05:59.890 --> 06:01.390
Probably being foisted...

06:01.660 --> 06:03.700
with a treasure map or something
equally dubious!

06:03.870 --> 06:05.460
D-Don't be silly!

06:05.630 --> 06:08.960
This place is famous for its bargains.

06:10.960 --> 06:12.920
Ah, l-look at these binoculars!

06:13.480 --> 06:14.816
These are the binoculars used by Columbus,

06:14.840 --> 06:18.680
when he discovered the American
continent, you know!

06:19.880 --> 06:22.010
Ehh? That's awesome.

06:22.280 --> 06:23.650
M-Master...

06:23.690 --> 06:24.690
Huh?

06:24.780 --> 06:31.080
I hate to contradict you, but I don't believe
binoculars were in use in Columbus' time...

06:31.140 --> 06:32.520
W-What?!

06:33.420 --> 06:35.460
Master, don't do it!

06:35.580 --> 06:38.290
This shop just reeks of farce, no
matter how you look at it.

06:39.310 --> 06:40.460
You think so?

06:40.670 --> 06:45.470
To upgrade the samurai show, I thought
I'd buy a Japanese sword.

06:45.670 --> 06:46.670
Oh, if that's the case!

06:52.580 --> 06:53.580
This is...

06:56.010 --> 06:58.380
the famous sword, Muramasa!

07:00.320 --> 07:03.610
What do you think of this sheen?
Magnificent, isn't it?

07:05.910 --> 07:06.990
What's so funny?

07:07.330 --> 07:10.080
Because! Look there!

07:10.200 --> 07:14.480
If that was a real Japanese sword, wouldn't
they write "Muramasa" in Japanese?

07:14.610 --> 07:17.900
There's no way it would be written
in the English alphabet!

07:18.740 --> 07:19.980
D-Damn you!

07:20.670 --> 07:23.880
You really were trying to sell me fakes!

07:24.660 --> 07:25.660
Hold it you!

07:25.700 --> 07:26.540
Please wait a minute. S-Stop a moment!

07:26.600 --> 07:29.240
I'll make you regret
your insolence! Graaaah!

07:32.330 --> 07:34.040
Eh? Nadja!

07:36.020 --> 07:38.110
If it isn't Nadja!

07:42.630 --> 07:46.750
You looked pretty good in that
dress last time. Bonjour.

07:50.700 --> 07:52.830
Who the heck is this rude fella?

07:54.830 --> 07:57.460
He's Mr. Fernando Gonzales
of the Gonzales Barony.

07:57.540 --> 08:00.920
Ah! He's the guy who forced Nadja
to dance at that party!

08:01.670 --> 08:03.760
Nadja, friends of yours?

08:03.830 --> 08:04.560
Yes...

08:04.600 --> 08:08.060
What a "unique" bunch of commoners.

08:08.110 --> 08:09.030
Same goes for you!

08:09.050 --> 08:13.770
For a baron like you to show up at a flea
market full of commoners, you're pretty strange!

08:15.120 --> 08:15.990
Well, actually...

08:16.020 --> 08:18.390
I come here for the occasional bargain.

08:18.480 --> 08:21.860
I consider this place to be a training
ground for appraising truly valuable objects.

08:22.650 --> 08:23.820
W-What an act.

08:23.940 --> 08:25.440
I'm getting hives.

08:25.550 --> 08:29.680
Well then, with the Baron's eye
for telling the real thing...

08:29.770 --> 08:32.280
why don't you find us a real bargain?

08:32.350 --> 08:33.350
Yeah, yeah.

08:33.490 --> 08:34.950
Let's see...

08:35.700 --> 08:37.749
TJ, good idea!

08:37.750 --> 08:38.750
Of course.

08:38.870 --> 08:40.620
Fine, follow me then.

08:51.680 --> 08:54.760
This place has a pretty nice collection.

08:56.270 --> 08:57.730
Especially this clock.

08:58.300 --> 09:01.630
It's old, but the intricate woodwork
gives it a nice look.

09:03.310 --> 09:07.080
You're young, but you have a good eye to
be able to see the merits of that clock.

09:07.190 --> 09:09.150
Wow, we should have expected as much.

09:09.450 --> 09:11.410
No... you flatter me.

09:11.840 --> 09:13.260
How should I say this...

09:13.750 --> 09:16.670
I've been surrounded by only valuable
things since I was a child.

09:17.120 --> 09:18.960
To calmly boast like that...

09:18.990 --> 09:19.990
Exactly!

09:20.050 --> 09:22.300
I'll take it, gramps.

09:22.330 --> 09:24.580
How much... for that clock?

09:26.100 --> 09:29.200
I'm sorry, but that clock is not for sale.

09:32.060 --> 09:33.860
You're a good businessman,
aren't you, gramps?

09:38.940 --> 09:41.520
I got it, I got it. I'll give
you 200 Francs for it.

09:44.710 --> 09:45.800
300 Francs!

09:46.590 --> 09:48.390
You shouldn't have anything
to complain about!

09:49.170 --> 09:52.010
It seems that I've given
you too much credit.

09:52.350 --> 09:53.350
What?!

09:53.750 --> 09:56.410
That clock isn't worth that much, and...

09:57.690 --> 09:58.940
It's broken and won't move.

09:59.230 --> 10:01.920
I thought as much!

10:04.130 --> 10:05.970
If that's the case,
don't put it in your shop!

10:06.150 --> 10:07.150
Young sir!

10:10.590 --> 10:13.010
This is as important...

10:13.300 --> 10:14.810
to me as my life.

10:15.470 --> 10:18.460
It's a memento that I could never
let go of, even for a moment.

10:21.190 --> 10:22.440
A memento...

10:22.790 --> 10:23.200
Heh!

10:23.730 --> 10:27.230
This rundown clock that doesn't
even work, a memento?

10:29.480 --> 10:30.650
How foolish!

11:02.060 --> 11:03.480
What was that for?!

11:04.460 --> 11:06.750
I don't even... Sorry!

11:07.770 --> 11:08.770
But...

11:09.230 --> 11:13.440
Everyone has precious memories
that can't be bought with money.

11:15.450 --> 11:17.330
To laugh at that...

11:17.700 --> 11:20.820
Geez, you commoners!

11:21.060 --> 11:22.310
The exit is this way!

11:22.810 --> 11:23.810
Get out of the way!

11:26.340 --> 11:28.840
Nadja, that was a nice move...

11:29.130 --> 11:30.360
Herbie!

11:32.920 --> 11:34.920
You're one interesting little lady!

11:35.010 --> 11:36.840
Come on... You too, gramps?

11:37.220 --> 11:38.720
Call me Gerard.

11:39.050 --> 11:41.430
It's my thanks for slapping him for me.

11:41.800 --> 11:43.770
Choose anything you like from the shop.

11:43.810 --> 11:45.180
It'll be a present.

11:45.710 --> 11:48.170
If he puts it that way, you better accept.

11:48.390 --> 11:49.440
It's proper etiquette.

11:49.800 --> 11:50.800
Y-Yes...

11:53.800 --> 11:55.280
Is there something interesting there?

11:55.380 --> 11:57.540
Wow... it's beautiful.

12:02.610 --> 12:06.780
Ah, it certainly does seem similar
somehow to my brooch.

12:14.090 --> 12:15.760
This melody is...

12:45.450 --> 12:47.830
It's the same music as back then...

12:54.630 --> 12:57.500
Mr. Gerard, is it really okay
for me to accept your offer?

12:57.580 --> 12:58.300
Yeah.

12:58.550 --> 13:00.260
Then, I'd like to have this.

13:00.590 --> 13:02.840
Oh, you sure have a sharp eye for things.

13:03.050 --> 13:04.600
But unfortunately...

13:04.760 --> 13:06.720
that isn't for sale either.

13:06.810 --> 13:09.350
You can have a pick
of anything else though.

13:09.670 --> 13:10.920
Is that right...

13:11.440 --> 13:12.440
Kennosuke.

13:12.480 --> 13:13.480
Yeah...

13:15.170 --> 13:16.600
Huh, where are you going?

13:16.760 --> 13:19.340
Oh my. Everyone's here.

13:19.620 --> 13:23.960
I'm on my way to buy materials
for your stage costumes.

13:24.030 --> 13:25.240
Come along with us!

13:25.320 --> 13:26.320
Okay!

13:26.680 --> 13:28.690
Mr. Gerard, I'll come back later!

13:28.870 --> 13:29.870
Yeah.

13:34.540 --> 13:36.500
Kennosuke, aren't you going?

13:36.710 --> 13:39.460
It's interesting here, I'll
be here a while longer.

13:45.540 --> 13:47.340
You're really into it, aren't you?

13:47.600 --> 13:48.600
Yeah.

13:48.720 --> 13:51.730
I absolutely love mechanics and machinery!

13:51.870 --> 13:52.740
I see...

13:52.870 --> 13:54.160
Hey, Mr. Gerard.

13:54.610 --> 13:58.490
Can you let me try fixing that clock?

13:58.610 --> 13:59.480
Hey, hey.

13:59.550 --> 14:02.130
It was hopeless no matter how
many times I tried to fix it.

14:02.150 --> 14:03.910
If you think it s hopeless...

14:04.410 --> 14:05.530
why don't you let me try!

14:07.100 --> 14:08.100
Okay.

14:08.330 --> 14:09.330
Thank you!

14:09.580 --> 14:10.870
You have tools and stuff, right?

14:15.730 --> 14:18.600
Whoa, you take good care of your tools.

14:22.590 --> 14:23.760
All right!

14:34.290 --> 14:35.540
Sylvie! Come here!

14:36.340 --> 14:37.340
Alright.

14:39.400 --> 14:40.400
What do you think?

14:41.800 --> 14:45.340
The rose design is beautiful,
and it feels good on my skin.

14:46.160 --> 14:47.990
Nadja! Rita, you too! Come over here.

14:51.120 --> 14:54.330
It suits Nadja and Rita as well.

14:54.570 --> 14:56.940
Really! It's cute and pretty!

14:58.920 --> 15:00.860
I'd like to take these three.

15:01.070 --> 15:03.570
As I expected madam,
you've got a sharp eye.

15:03.790 --> 15:05.940
These are the best goods in my shop!

15:06.380 --> 15:08.050
The total will be 6 francs.

15:08.280 --> 15:09.720
What did you say?!

15:09.870 --> 15:13.500
Unfortunately, I only have
this much with me...

15:15.440 --> 15:16.440
Yes...

15:17.110 --> 15:20.650
The three of them looked so happy,
and to think I can't get them...

15:20.920 --> 15:23.820
Aaah, they'll be so disappointed!

15:24.600 --> 15:27.580
I-I get it... If you feel so strongly
about it, then...

15:27.620 --> 15:29.620
What you have on you will be enough.

15:30.640 --> 15:34.160
Oh~! I thought your goods were fine,
but the shop owner is wonderful too!

15:34.190 --> 15:35.700
Well then, if you please.

15:41.210 --> 15:42.840
That was a relief wasn't it, Granny?

15:43.030 --> 15:44.400
Now then...

15:45.010 --> 15:48.550
Next, let's look for men's materials.

15:48.740 --> 15:50.200
But we have no more...

15:52.410 --> 15:54.750
Here, I've brought another purse you see!

15:56.980 --> 16:00.440
I'd love to show Granny to that Baron!

16:04.430 --> 16:07.020
It may be a bit early, but before
the restaurants get crowded,

16:07.140 --> 16:08.420
why don't we have lunch?

16:08.510 --> 16:09.510
You're right.

16:10.030 --> 16:12.370
Well, I'll go call Kennosuke then.

16:16.540 --> 16:17.540
Alright!

16:17.790 --> 16:19.420
All done!

16:22.320 --> 16:24.200
Mr. Gerard, try moving it now.

16:24.970 --> 16:25.970
Okay...

16:35.020 --> 16:36.890
I-It's working!

16:37.230 --> 16:39.020
I think the cuckoo will move too.

16:42.840 --> 16:44.820
That clock... it's all fixed now!

16:45.210 --> 16:47.000
With my skills...

16:47.040 --> 16:48.710
it wasn't a problem!

16:49.200 --> 16:50.780
That's great isn't it?

16:51.120 --> 16:52.120
Mr. Ge-...

16:52.600 --> 16:53.680
This clock is...

16:54.160 --> 16:58.000
the only thing I ever gave my
wife besides the wedding ring.

16:59.460 --> 17:00.630
My wife...

17:02.250 --> 17:03.700
For 50 years...

17:04.040 --> 17:06.520
she wiped it clean everyday...

17:07.120 --> 17:08.540
and wound it up.

17:11.760 --> 17:14.220
She really treasured it to the very end.

17:14.720 --> 17:17.430
By 'very end', you mean, your wife...

17:18.270 --> 17:21.140
She went to heaven... three years ago.

17:21.690 --> 17:25.440
It stopped moving exactly
when my wife died.

17:26.230 --> 17:30.110
It must have contained your wife's
spirit who treasured it so.

17:30.150 --> 17:33.910
It's said people who treasure things,
treasure their memories.

17:34.030 --> 17:35.870
She must have been a wonderful wife.

17:36.120 --> 17:39.950
I'm a stubborn old man, and made her worry.

17:40.660 --> 17:43.120
But she just smiled and supported
whatever I did.

17:45.060 --> 17:47.110
She was a better wife than I deserved...

17:51.510 --> 17:53.340
Thank you, Kennosuke!

17:56.970 --> 17:59.390
Thank you very much, Kennosuke.

17:59.640 --> 18:03.540
Aww... I'm glad it made you happy.
It makes me happy, too.

18:03.850 --> 18:04.850
For my gratitude...

18:04.980 --> 18:08.070
Kennosuke with the little lady,
both of you pick out what you want.

18:08.760 --> 18:09.880
How about this?

18:10.040 --> 18:12.880
It's a pretty well made
silver pocket watch!

18:13.240 --> 18:14.740
Say, Mr. Gerard...

18:17.830 --> 18:18.950
That music box...

18:19.160 --> 18:23.040
It doesn't seem to be related to your
late wife... can't you give it away?

18:23.210 --> 18:24.540
Hmm... That...

18:25.370 --> 18:30.340
It was when my wife was still
alive, about ten years ago.

18:35.340 --> 18:37.010
Her dress was simple, but...

18:37.300 --> 18:41.310
There was a grace about the lady who
came to the shop with her baby.

18:42.180 --> 18:43.850
It's a pretty fine piece.

18:44.310 --> 18:45.850
I'll buy it for 20 francs.

18:46.270 --> 18:48.520
Dear, be a little more reasonable.

18:50.070 --> 18:52.490
Well I'll be generous, 50 francs.

18:52.530 --> 18:53.860
Oh my, that much?

18:53.900 --> 18:55.420
I'm glad for you.

18:55.450 --> 18:56.780
Thank you very much.

19:01.830 --> 19:05.960
Excuse me... Can you let me hear
the music box one last time?

19:06.620 --> 19:09.250
That's fine. It's a special
song for you, isn't it?

19:09.380 --> 19:10.380
Dear...

19:10.410 --> 19:11.410
Yeah.

19:16.840 --> 19:22.060
It seems that it was the first song that
she and her late husband danced to.

19:26.310 --> 19:28.940
This held a wonderful memory for you.

19:28.980 --> 19:29.980
Yeah.

19:30.110 --> 19:31.360
Say, dear.

19:31.520 --> 19:34.490
Let's hold on to this
music box for a while.

19:35.360 --> 19:37.780
It's holding someone's wonderful memories.

19:37.990 --> 19:40.580
Someday, she might come and buy it back.

19:40.620 --> 19:41.620
Yes.

19:42.700 --> 19:45.080
That was a wonderful story too.

19:45.120 --> 19:47.709
But you said it was over
10 years ago, didn't you?

19:47.710 --> 19:50.419
If she hasn't come back to buy
it back in all this time...

19:50.420 --> 19:53.919
That lady might have forgotten
about it already.

19:53.920 --> 19:56.800
I'd like to believe
that it isn't so, but...

20:02.010 --> 20:04.180
I'll give that to you, little lady.

20:04.420 --> 20:07.740
Eh? But that person might come
back to buy this back.

20:08.480 --> 20:10.100
I'm getting older, and...

20:10.490 --> 20:12.990
I could go to be with my wife anytime.

20:14.280 --> 20:17.280
In that case, I don't know where
this music box might end up.

20:17.900 --> 20:21.160
If so, I'd rather it be given to someone
who would treasure it.

20:21.910 --> 20:22.910
But...

20:22.990 --> 20:24.040
Open it.

20:25.410 --> 20:28.080
Your face, when you were listening
to that music box,

20:28.370 --> 20:31.830
I felt it was somehow similar
to that lady's face.

20:35.760 --> 20:37.760
That baby the lady held...

20:37.920 --> 20:40.430
would be just about your age, too.

20:41.260 --> 20:42.760
This must be fate.

20:43.260 --> 20:44.890
Please take care of it.

20:46.620 --> 20:48.040
Thank you very much!

20:48.640 --> 20:50.390
That's great, Nadja.

20:50.730 --> 20:51.730
Yes.

20:56.280 --> 21:00.170
Vienna House of Count Waltmuller

21:10.370 --> 21:11.460
I'm sorry...

21:11.870 --> 21:14.250
I promised not to play this song again...

21:15.210 --> 21:16.420
It's all right, Collette.

21:18.090 --> 21:22.640
I know that this was a special song between
you and your late husband.

21:23.180 --> 21:24.890
Please, let me hear the rest.

21:25.510 --> 21:26.260
But...

21:26.470 --> 21:28.270
I like this song too.

21:28.850 --> 21:30.180
Just as much as you.

21:57.630 --> 22:00.090
This music that Francis and I danced to...

22:00.470 --> 22:02.790
To have danced to it with her
husband for the first time...

22:03.050 --> 22:04.970
I wonder what kind of lady she was.

22:15.370 --> 22:16.995
Paris is sunnier than London

22:16.996 --> 22:18.620
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

22:18.740 --> 22:21.830
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

22:22.250 --> 22:25.335
The Queen of Spades is a fickle person

22:25.336 --> 22:28.420
SUPEEDO no jou kimagure yasan

22:29.380 --> 22:30.620
- Indeed
- Kitto

22:33.380 --> 22:35.800
- It's not use worrying about it
- Nayan datte MUDA yo

22:36.380 --> 22:37.945
Que sera sera, sera Sera

22:37.946 --> 22:39.510
KE SERA SERA SERA SERA

22:39.770 --> 22:42.125
Tomorrow's going to
be whatever it was meant

22:42.126 --> 22:44.480
Ashita nante itsumo naru you ni

22:44.560 --> 22:45.940
- To be, to be
- Naru naru

22:46.270 --> 22:48.775
The tree fog won

22:48.776 --> 22:51.280
Sekai KAERU tobi KONKUURU

22:51.740 --> 22:53.700
The world frog-jumping contest

22:53.701 --> 22:55.660
Yuushou shita yo AMAGAERU

22:58.870 --> 23:01.955
Under the kitten's paw

23:01.956 --> 23:05.040
Koneko chan no ashi no ura wa

23:05.460 --> 23:08.545
Is the scent of the sun, right?

23:08.546 --> 23:11.630
Otentou sama no nioi dane

23:14.470 --> 23:16.135
Paris is sunnier than London

23:16.136 --> 23:17.800
RONDON don yori haretara PARI

23:17.890 --> 23:20.890
- Carmen likes paella more than pasta
- CARUMEN men yori PAERIYA suki

23:21.390 --> 23:24.580
It's not the time to hang around

23:24.581 --> 23:27.770
Michikusa shite iru baai ja nai ne

23:28.650 --> 23:30.900
Indeed, indeed

23:30.901 --> 23:33.150
Kitto kitto

23:41.500 --> 23:42.920
- Tomorrow's Nadja
- Tomorrow's Nadja

23:42.940 --> 23:44.610
Huh? Aren't you Oliver?!

23:44.780 --> 23:46.400
To be meeting in a place like this...

23:46.450 --> 23:48.490
Let me introduce him to you, everyone.

23:48.610 --> 23:50.660
He's from Applefield Orphanage too.

23:51.230 --> 23:53.400
Huh? What's the matter, Oliver?

23:53.620 --> 23:56.040
Your face is all red. Do you have a fever?

23:56.800 --> 23:58.206
Just when we were getting reacquainted,

23:58.230 --> 24:00.650
Rosso and Bianco appeared before us.

24:01.190 --> 24:03.280
Oliver, come and escape with me!

24:03.980 --> 24:04.900
Tomorrow's Nadja:

24:04.940 --> 24:06.970
Crisis Point!! A Confession in Paris.

24:05.040 --> 24:07.239
Crisis Point!!
A Confession in Paris.

24:07.240 --> 24:08.980
Now, the Door of Destiny opens.
